  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "What is a deque?"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A deque (pronounced deck), or double-ended queue, is an ordered linear list in which elements can be inserted and deleted at either end, FRONT or REAR. If insertion and deletion are done at the same end it behaves like a stack; if they are done at opposite ends it behaves like a queue. Applications include re-joining a queue at the front, vehicles moving to the rear of another lane at a toll booth, keeping a browser history or undo list of limited size, and checking whether a string is a palindrome."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Insert and delete at both ends"
    },
    {
     "en": "Same end → stack (LIFO)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Opposite ends → queue (FIFO)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Uses: limited history, undo, palindrome check"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A deque (pronounced deck), or double-ended queue, is an ordered linear list in which elements can be inserted and deleted at either end, FRONT or REAR. If insertion and deletion are done at the same end it behaves like a stack; if they are done at opposite ends it behaves like a queue. Applications include re-joining a queue at the front, vehicles moving to the rear of another lane at a toll booth, keeping a browser history or undo list of limited size, and checking whether a string is a palindrome.",
    "kn": "ಡೆಕ್ ಅಥವಾ ಎರಡು ತುದಿಯ ಕ್ಯೂನಲ್ಲಿ FRONT ಮತ್ತು REAR ಎರಡೂ ತುದಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಸೇರಿಸಬಹುದು ಮತ್ತು ತೆಗೆಯಬಹುದು. ಒಂದೇ ತುದಿ ಬಳಸಿದರೆ ಸ್ಟ್ಯಾಕ್, ಬೇರೆ ತುದಿಗಳು ಬಳಸಿದರೆ ಕ್ಯೂ."
   }
  },
